    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0270" n="260" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg260"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/12–3149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Australia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jarman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canberra</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-12-31T13:00:00+10:00">December 31,
                            1949—1 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 31—5:11 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>282. External Affairs official told Foster<anchor n="24" xml:id="d290-f1"/> late
                    Friday (Embtel December 30, 3 p. m.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d290-f2"/>) that
                    Australian Government has taken definite decision re recognition Communists’
                    Government China and has communicated decision to London.</p>
                <p>Official added that External Affairs not now at liberty reveal decision to US,
                    but would ask Spender’s<anchor n="26" xml:id="d290-f3"/> permission.</p>
                <p>Delayed sending this message hoping to receive information. Definitely refused
                    this morning. Private and confidential information secured from Office New
                    Zealand High Commissioner to effect Australian Government decision taken before
                    Christmas was to note UK recognition on January 2 without approval and not to
                    recognize now; this apparently in line with NZ action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jarman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d290-f1" n="24" xml:id="d290-f1-content">
                <p>Andrew B. Foster, Counselor of Embassy in Australia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d290-f2" n="25" xml:id="d290-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d290-f3" n="26" xml:id="d290-f3-content">
                <p>Percy C. Spender, Australian Minister for External Affairs and External
                    Territories.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
